# kernel-tile.img -- Linux 4.14.311 for TILE-Gx, one tile under qemu
#
# Runs on qemu-system-tilegx -M tilegx from the qemu fork (lordrasmus/qemu,
# branch uclibc-ng); upstream qemu had TILE-Gx as linux-user only and dropped
# it in 6.0.  The image is vmlinux (ELF, stripped).
#
#   qemu-system-tilegx -M tilegx -m 512M -nographic -kernel kernel-tile.img \
#     -initrd rootfs.img.xz -append console=hvc0
#
# A TILE-Gx kernel is a client of the Tilera hypervisor and touches no device
# of its own.  qemu serves the hypervisor calls itself: the console (hvc0),
# memory, page tables, the RTC, -append as the command line, and -initrd as
# the hvfs file "initramfs", which the kernel loads in load_hv_initrd().
# The machine has one tile and its RAM from physical address 0; -m must be a
# multiple of 16 MiB.
#
# Patches against linux-4.14.311:
#   kernel-tile-loop-distribute.patch  memcpy recursed into itself with gcc 10
#   kernel-readahead-tmpfs.patch       readahead(2) on tmpfs (shared with
#                                      cris; applies with an offset)
#
# Build:
#
#   cd linux-4.14.311
#   patch -p1 < kernel-tile-loop-distribute.patch
#   patch -p1 < kernel-readahead-tmpfs.patch
#   cp kernel-tile.config .config
#   make ARCH=tile CROSS_COMPILE=tilegx-openadk-linux-uclibc- \
#        HOSTCFLAGS="-fcommon -std=gnu11" olddefconfig vmlinux
#   tilegx-openadk-linux-uclibc-strip -o kernel-tile.img vmlinux
#
# Toolchain: toolchain-tilegx-gcc-10.5.0-no-static.
# HOSTCFLAGS: 4.14's dtc needs -fcommon, and scripts/unifdef.c does not build
# as C23, which gcc 15 picks by default.
# The config is tilegx_defconfig without PCI, USB, the GXIO devices and
# modules, NR_CPUS=2, KERNEL_PL=2, 64 KiB pages.
#
# Result with the CI's static rootfs: 315 passed, 22 failed, 9 skipped; the
# failures are the FP exception and rounding mode checks, which TILE-Gx cannot
# meet (no FPU, no FP status register; gcc inlines fdouble_*/fsingle_*).
